"\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n## Review\nThis is the village of Leura, which we stopped at for lunch on the way back from the Featherdale Wildlife Park and Blue Mountains tour.  \nHaving searched ahead before arriving in town, we were able to head straight to the restaurant as soon as we got there.  \n\nWe ordered TURKISH CHILLI SCRAMBLED EGGS and DOUBLE CHEESEBURGER.  \nNothing on the menu stood out, so after a long deliberation we settled on the safe-looking burger.  \n\nThe burger came with fries, and the staff asked about our choice of sauce.  \nNothing came to mind, so we asked for a recommendation and they showed us the options directly.  \nWe were curious about BBQ sauce but were wondering if it would pair well with fries — the staff said it was a good choice, so we went with BBQ sauce.  \nIt actually went surprisingly well with the fries, and we were happy with it.  \n\nAfter the meal, we asked about dessert as well, but it was raining outside and the timing was awkward — too in-between for a separate cafe trip — so we ordered coffee instead.  \nIt turned out the person taking our dessert order was Korean, so being able to order comfortably in Korean was a pleasant surprise.  \n\nOverall, it was a great spot to unwind after the tour.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"